;; perf-ext — the things that are NOT "observe a running JVM":
;;   diagnose  compile-time cost notes   (different input, different lifecycle)
;;   control   trace + JDI restarts      (a debugger)
;;   native    FFM safety tiers          (a different domain)
;;   flow      FlowStorm bridge          (an optional peer tool)
;;   trace     Sayid bridge              (function value tracing)
;;   remote    JDI over a socket         (the CDT architecture)
;;   nrepl     the op-contract seam      (source-loaded middleware, not AOT'd)
;; They ride on perf's model but are not needed to use it. AOT'd into the
;; always-on jar they would load on every JVM start, so they are opt-in.
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {dev/perf {:local/root "../perf"}}}
